; energy_scales_with_model (QUI-1056): pins the step cost of an ENERGY walk
; over a model whose coefficients the program itself wrote.
;
; A 4-variable binary model gets four SETLINE writes (13 steps each, per
; spec/xqvm/METERING.md's COEFF_WRITE_STEPS), a matching 4-element sample
; (1 step per element via SAMPLE_COPY_STEPS), and one ENERGY over both
; (model_eval_steps = sample_len*SAMPLE_COPY_STEPS + terms*MODEL_TERM_STEPS).
; This vector asserts both implementations charge the same total for that
; walk, not just that they agree on the resulting energy.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0

PUSH 0
PUSH 1
SETLINE r0
PUSH 1
PUSH 2
SETLINE r0
PUSH 2
PUSH 3
SETLINE r0
PUSH 3
PUSH 4
SETLINE r0

PUSH 4
BSMX r1

ENERGY r0 r1
STOW r2
PUSH 0
OUTPUT r2
HALT
